-- title:
--   Descent along Spec(B ⊗ 𝒪̂^{nr}) → Spec B: epimorphism
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, together with an irreducible element $\pi \in \mathcal O$ such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$. Let $\mathrm{Onr}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and let $\mathrm{Fr}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $\mathrm{Onr}$, subject to: $\mathrm{Onr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every $x \in \mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod \pi$ for all $x$. Let $m > 0$, let $S =$ `AlgHom.equalizer` of $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$ and the identity (the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$-fixed elements), and let $\mathrm{FrS}$ be an $S$-algebra automorphism of $\mathrm{Onr}$ whose underlying map is $\mathrm{Fr}^{m}$. Let $B$ be a commutative ring that is simultaneously an $\mathcal O$-algebra and an $S$-algebra, compatibly, in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent. Then for every scheme $T$ and all morphisms $g_1, g_2 \colon \operatorname{Spec} B \to T$, if the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}(B \otimes_{S} \mathrm{Onr}) \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ induced by $b \mapsto b \otimes 1$ composed with $g_1$ equals the same morphism composed with $g_2$, then $g_1 = g_2$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness, or epimorphism, half of the scalar-descent step for the Čerednik–Drinfeld formal upper half-plane: the projection $\operatorname{Spec}(B \otimes_{S} \hat{\mathcal O}^{\mathrm{nr}}) \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ is an epimorphism of schemes whenever $\pi$ is nilpotent in $B$, so that a morphism out of $\operatorname{Spec} B$ is determined by its pullback to the unramified base change. It is used, together with the affine descent statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.existsUnique_tmul_one_eq_of_map_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.existsUnique_tmul_one_eq_of_map_frobenius_eq), by the existence and existence-and-uniqueness results for descending a Frobenius-equivariant morphism from $\operatorname{Spec}(B \otimes_{S} \hat{\mathcal O}^{\mathrm{nr}})$ to $\operatorname{Spec} B$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalOmega_eq_of_specMap_includeLeft_comp_eq_of_isNilpotent.lean

